Z||000010||Jefrysuko||11-29-2001||03:30 AM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.stopstart.fsnet.co.uk/smilie/stupid.gif">  <P>Please don't take offense Smooth.  I'm not calling you stupid, I have just been waiting for an occasion to use that smiley.<P>I will admit that BlackStang does not appear to have the social skills to behave in an appropriate manner on this forum and most likely not in society either.  We all know that Cliff wants this to be a public place and is very tolerant with these types of matters and I respect that very much.  I do however agree that it would be good to call his attention to this matter.  Considering the fact that two of BlackStang's threads have gone over 30 posts I would believe that Cliff is already watching.  But then again when isn't Cliff watching?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>Edit:  Because I forgot how to do smileys  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Jefrysuko (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Nashco||11-29-2001||03:30 AM||||I've bit my tongue (metaphorically) WAAAY too much.  I can't take too much more of him either; it's ridiculous, unnecessary, and spreading like wildfire.  Amazing how such an old saying like, "One bad apple can spoil the whole bunch," still applies to modern day things...huh?<P>Cliff, I know you try to be fair, but this is just getting outright rude.  You see what goes on, I know, and I'm sure you have your moments of anger and laughter.  Please...he's obviously not going to change his antics and has not offered a good thing to the forum yet, as far as I've seen.  He now thinks if he starts a post with, "You're cool, but..." or, "Yeah, that may be true, but..." and similar statements that whatever follows the BUT is alright.  I know I'm not fooled by this little show of fake friendliness, and it further adds to my anger.<P>If no action will be taken with him directly, I sure hope that voting system comes around soon, if you do plan on making it.<P>Thanks for your time reading this Cliff, and I could not express in words how thankful I am that you moderate and manage this forum; without you, many of us would be lost.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000012||AgaricX||11-29-2001||03:43 AM||||I HATE HATE flame wars... I know from moderating computer tech support message boards for years...<P>(its amazing how bad Apple/Mac ppl hate PC ppl)<P>I have read many many posts by BlackStang... and honestly I get a laught sometimes... but more often than not I end up rolling my eyes.<P>I mean SERIOUSLY... we've had MANY discussions with MR2 owners who post here and I find most of those posts educational and very enjoyable.  I'm not saying axe him... but you might want to consider it.  This is for information and discussion... not a ****  waving competition (please excuse the crude analogy).<P>Thats my 2 cents<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.agaric.net/fiero/AgaricX.jpg">  <BR>'85 SE 3800SC 5 Spd<BR>I WANT A FASTBACK!!!||||reg||13
Z||000013||Cliff Pennock||11-29-2001||05:34 AM||||I've received quite a few complaints about him lately so let's just say he's on the "a few more complaints and he's outta here" list already.<P>But let's be honest, he's getting waaaaay too much attention waaaaay to easy. I haven't read any of his messages lately, simply because I always skip his messages when I encounter them in a thread. Sorry if this offends you BlackStang, but I find the signal-to-noise ratio in your messages quite low, so the skipping has become somewhat automatic. I mean, <B>in my opinion</B> most of your messages (that I've read anyway) are just trolling attempts and should be ignored. I wish more people would do that.<P>But putting my personal feelings aside for a moment, he <B>is</B> nearing the point of being banned. As most of you know by now, I use two criteria when banning people. The first is the number of times somebody is "violating" the few rules set out on this forum. The second is the number of complaints I receive from people. BlackStang isn't violating much of the rules (anymore) other than using colorful language. But the number of complaints I've been receiving is steadily rising.<P>So BlackStang, I <B>would</B> practice a bit more caution here if I were you. Not because <B>they</B> are right and <B>you</B> are wrong, but because more and more people are starting to find your posts increasingly offensive. It's alright to disagree with people, it's the way you word your disagreements that's rubbing people the wrong way.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Monkeyman||11-29-2001||05:38 AM||||I've just wasted the last 30 minutes reading the Dale Earnhart (Jeff Gordon fan here, BTW  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) and CoolBlue threads just to see what all of the hubbub was all about.  Here are my comments.<P>BlackStang--You seem to be an instigator.  Please stop for your own sake.  You tend to annoy almost everyone on PFF.  I don't know why you do this, but it's not the way to make friends and influence people.  (BTW--This has nothing to do with what you drive.  I couldn't care less.)<P>SmooothGT--You're right that BlackStang is out of line, but I think it would have been a little more appropriate to just email Cliff.  Starting a thread is just adding fuel to the fire.<P>If it were me, I'd give BlackStang a "time out".  30 days without access to the forum or something.  Let him consider what he's done and if he really wants to be a part of the group.<P>Last but not least, all of this flaming is getting boring and old really fast.  When I joined a couple of years ago, things were nice and quiet.  Others have left because of the constant bickering.  Maybe it's time for me to go, too.||||reg||1
