Z||000043||Oreif||11-29-2001||07:00 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>"BS95 started spouting incorrect information and when his information was proven wrong, he attempted to "flame" his way out of it."<P>It's information I read from an impartial source, not a fiero fanatic.  You mentioned a book that I'd never heard of, while I showed a link.  Who proved who wrong?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Well see there you go, If you were ANY kind of "car guy" you should know the author of the book. Gary Witzenburg has a series of books where he has went over the entire history of cars. From engineering idea all the the year he finished the book. The Fiero book was one. He has done one for the Firebirds, Camaros, Mustangs, and Cougars.<BR>(He has done others but they are out of print) All his facts are from factory records not from some obscure Fiero website out of Sweden. Maybe you should go to a library and see if they have the Mustang book. You could at least learn about the history of the car you drive.<BR>It's called:<P>MUSTANG-THE COMPLETE HISTORY OF AMERICA'S PONY CAR by Gary Witzenburg (pub. 1979)<P>You can get it at:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.amazon.com" TARGET=_blank>www.amazon.com</A> <P>Just type in the author's name and you'll see five of his books are still available including the Fiero book.<P>I bet many here already know about or even have this book already. But you being the "car guy" you are, don't need a book, You already know all.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-29-2001).]||||reg||1
